{"id":"chatcmpl-56a39d5d-62ef-40c0-bdfa-3d93306c3a15","object":"chat.completion","created":1795248684,"model":"deepseek-v4.1-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","reasoning_content":"","content":"{\n  \"highlights\": \"When a direct expert query yields a negative or ambiguous result but the task implies a finding exists, escalate to complementary localization tools that provide spatial coordinates. Use image laterality markers to map image coordinates to patient anatomy, ensuring correct side attribution. Cross-validate findings across multiple tools before committing to an answer.\",\n  \"patterns\": [\n    \"When a primary expert tool returns 'no finding' but the question presupposes a finding, switch to a localization or grounding tool that can detect subtle abnormalities.\",\n    \"When a tool provides image coordinates, always map them to patient anatomy using laterality markers (e.g., 'L' marker) to avoid left/right confusion.\",\n    \"When multiple tools give conflicting results, prioritize the tool that directly addresses the specific finding in question (e.g., rib deformity) over general-purpose tools.\",\n    \"When the answer requires laterality (left vs. right), explicitly verify the side using coordinate-based localization rather than relying on textual descriptions alone.\"\n  ],\n  \"playbooks\": {\n    \"Medical Imaging\": \"Use expert tools for initial assessment, but if negative or ambiguous, employ grounding tools to localize specific findings and confirm laterality with image markers.\",\n    \"Visual Question Answering\": \"When options imply a finding exists, don't stop at a negative expert response; use coordinate-based grounding to detect and localize the finding.\",\n    \"Radiology\": \"Always cross-check laterality by mapping image coordinates to patient anatomy using radiological markers (e.g., 'L' for left side).\"\n  },\n  \"checklists\": [\n    \"Confirm that the tool used directly addresses the finding in question (e.g., rib deformity) rather than a related but different finding (e.g., lung opacity).\",\n    \"Verify laterality by checking image markers and coordinate positions before finalizing the answer.\"\n  ]\n}"},"finish_reason":"stop","logprobs":null}],"usage":{"prompt_tokens":520,"total_tokens":901,"completion_tokens":381,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":0,"image_tokens":0,"text_tokens":520},"completion_tokens_details":{"text_tokens":381}}}